n by **name**, not by id. Deleting or renaming a partition is not checked against the deployments that use it, so update those deployments' `defaultBatchJobConfig.partition` as well."," "," ### Deleting"," ","@@ -213,4 +213,4 @@ Deployments refer to a partition by **name**, not by id. Deleting or renaming a"," "," ## How runs use this"," ","-When a run is launched, Airavata logs in to the cluster's head node under the run's **cluster config**. It creates the work directory under the config's work root, stages the run's data into it, writes the batch script and submits it with `sbatch` to the deployment's partition. The `#SBATCH` header is built from the run's resource request, including its allocation. See [application.md](application.md) for how deployments and runs are put together.","+When a run is launched, Airavata logs in to the cluster's head node under the run's **cluster config**. It creates the work directory under the config's work root, stages the run's data into it, writes the batch script and submits it with `sbatch` to the run's partition. The `#SBATCH` header is built from the run's resource request, including its allocation. See [application.md](application.md) for how deployments and runs are put together."],"additions":4,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/mcp.md","lines":["@@ -135,6 +135,6 @@ It shows each pending login and reads secret answers without echo."," ## Not available yet"," "," These need changes to `airavata-server` (Part B of the plan): registering applications as a non-admin, listing","-your earlier runs, cancelling a run, reading job logs, choosing a partition per run, keeping sbatch options the","+your earlier runs, cancelling a run, reading job logs, keeping sbatch options the"," API has no field for, workflows (predefined recipes such as sweeps and chains, which job arrays and dependency"," chains will map to, and Nextflow pipelines), searching data by metadata, and browsing a storage."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"t